        "She takes a flask from an inner pocket, unscrews it, drinks, offers. The offer is new. You take it or you do not; either way the smell is cheap rye that has never been in a brochure. If you drink, it burns the sweetness on your tongue and does not win. If you refuse, she nods and drinks your share, a small theft she allows herself.\n\n\"I trained a man in '09 who took the double and the conversion and the senator and then bought a boat,\" she says. \"The boat was real. The country with trees was a brochure. He sent me a postcard with no return. I burned it. I still know the front by heart. Do not send me a postcard. Send me a door that opens on you still answering to {{name}}.\" The flask vanishes. The story stays, a warning dressed as folklore.",
        "You ask, because you are still a person who asks, whether she would have refused Vale. She looks at the junction box as if it had asked instead. \"I would have refused and they would have run a smaller bag and I would have carried forced in my teeth to a rain deck and bitten someone who deserved it. Or I would have asked for the large knife because I was tired of being one animal. I have been tired that way. It is not a virtue. It is just tired.\"\n\nThe honesty, if you gave it, sits warmer in the room. The lie sits colder. The double sits like a third flask, unopened. She does not ask you to recant. She buttons her coat. \"Upstairs. I will talk on the deck where the rain can ruin a microphone. Then you will go home and not come. If you need to come, do it with your own hand and do not call it aftercare. Aftercare is how they get a second session into you without a wafer.\"",
