        "\"One more name.\" She does not say Mia as if it were a secret. She says it as if it were a live wire. \"You will want to see her before the gala. You will want a civilian to tell you you are still kind. Kind is a resource Helix harvests. If you go, you go clean — no stack-talk, no Vale, no coat that looks like a gift. If you do not go, I will not call you cruel. I will call you late. Late is survivable. Cruel to a pediatric nurse is a file Crowe already knows how to open.\"\n\nYou think of the unopened joke. The drawer. The flower on the grate. Voss watches the thought move across your face and does not steal it. That is the code again, or the leak.\n\n\"If they have already photographed you with her,\" she says, \"we are in a different math. Tell me if we are. Don't tell me later when the math has a van.\" You tell her the truth you have about Mia: protected, hinted, or silent, whichever flag you actually carry, in adult sentences. She files. The file is a kind of care. Care is a kind of cuff.",
        "A man of about forty hurries past with a dripping case and does not look at two people under an ad. Voss tracks him anyway, leftover field. When he is gone she is only your handler again. \"You are going to hate the next week,\" she says. \"Hate is clean. Hold it. If it turns into wanting Vale's building again — the meaning he is not licensed to treat — you call me before you call them. That is the last rail I can offer that is not a mission. I am offering it because I have watched Subject Zero smile in a way that made me want to hit a priest. I will not watch you learn that smile if I can still subtract.\"\n\nThe rain thickens on its playlist. She looks up as if she could see the grid's decision. \"Go home. Eat. Do not drink Helix's idea of tea. Tomorrow the dress. Then Mia if you dare. Then the gala. I will be in the van. You will be in the light. That is the job. I still think I can pull you out. If I stop thinking it I will tell you, once, and then I will run you like Kane. You do not want me to become Kane. Kane sleeps.\"",
